.TH MAKI-ATTACH 8
.SH NAME
maki-attach \- manage the NBD, LVM and XFS attachment for a Maki volume
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B maki-attach
.I action
.B \-\-volume
.I name
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-plan ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B attach
connects the NBD device and mounts the configured filesystem.
.B verify
checks the identity of the existing attachment.
.B grow
requires
.BI \-\-size-bytes " bytes"
and a verified, mounted attachment.
.PP
Stop workloads before running
.BR detach ", " recover " or " cleanup .
Use
.B recover
for a disconnected backend.
.B cleanup
uses the attachment record to select detach or recovery.
.B recover-failed-start
is the systemd failed-start cleanup hook.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Read attachment settings from this file. The default path, when present, is
.IR /etc/maki/attach/name.toml .
.TP
.B \-\-plan
Print the planned steps. Execution requires Linux and the volume identity.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR maki (8),
.BR maki-check (8)
